{{also|pull-out|pullout}}
==English==

===Verb===
'''[[pull]] [[out]]''' (of)

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[withdraw]]; especially of [[military]] [[forces]]; to [[retreat]].
#: ''The troops '''pulled out''' of the conflict.''
# {{context|literally|lang=en}} To use [[coitus interruptus]] as a method of [[birth control]].
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[remove]] something from a container.
#: ''He '''pulled out''' his gun before she had a chance to scream.''
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[maneuver]] a vehicle from the side of a road onto the [[lane]].
#: ''When joining a road, you should check for traffic before '''pulling out'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|removing something from a container}} [[whip out]]

